WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:16.905
Henry exclaimed, staring at Cole.

2
00:00:16.925 --> 00:00:21.509
"What do you mean, you put the lollipop in Daisy's pocket?

3
00:00:22.249 --> 00:00:25.392
Why?" Cole shrugged, looking sheepish.

4
00:00:25.412 --> 00:00:29.476
"I knew that Daisy loves those blueberry lollipops from the Dessert Den.

5
00:00:30.568 --> 00:00:33.651
She couldn't stop talking about them when I saw her there yesterday.

6
00:00:34.591 --> 00:00:39.295
So I decided to surprise her with one as a um good luck gift.

7
00:00:40.376 --> 00:00:43.479
I waited until she left to get some lemonade," he continued.

8
00:00:43.499 --> 00:00:48.162
"Then I sneaked into the barn and stuck a lollipop in the pocket of her show shirt."

9
00:00:49.223 --> 00:00:49.804
"You did?"

10
00:00:50.124 --> 00:00:50.785
Henry said.

11
00:00:50.805 --> 00:00:54.227
"Why? You didn't get Maggie anything.

12
00:00:54.948 --> 00:00:56.169
She likes candy too."

13
00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.930
"That's different."

14
00:00:58.631 --> 00:00:59.712
Cole looked embarrassed.

15
00:01:00.424 --> 00:01:02.085
"Maggie's just Maggie.

16
00:01:03.066 --> 00:01:07.088
Daisy is, you know, really nice and pretty and smart."

17
00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:09.869
"Oh!" Henry thought.

18
00:01:09.889 --> 00:01:13.191
"Cole has a crush on Daisy!"

19
00:01:13.211 --> 00:01:16.773
"Is that why you skipped swim team practice today?"

20
00:01:17.093 --> 00:01:17.633
he asked.

21
00:01:17.653 --> 00:01:19.414
"Because of Daisy?

22
00:01:20.195 --> 00:01:21.596
You wanted to watch her compete?"

23
00:01:21.616 --> 00:01:24.217
"Maybe." Cole shrugged.

24
00:01:24.797 --> 00:01:26.638
"I mean, I wanted to help you guys too."

25
00:01:26.658 --> 00:01:29.360
"Okay," Henry said.

26
00:01:30.116 --> 00:01:31.717
"So what happened with the shirt?

27
00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:33.978
Did you leave it in the water trough?"

28
00:01:34.938 --> 00:01:36.199
"No!" Cole said.

29
00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:39.560
"I just put the lollipop in Daisy's shirt pocket.

30
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.801
Then I left it hanging in the barn by Coco's stall."

31
00:01:42.821 --> 00:01:49.724
"When you said you were looking for more napkins, you were really hanging out with Daisy," Henry guessed.

32
00:01:49.744 --> 00:01:52.946
"That's when you put the lollipop in her pocket."

33
00:01:53.766 --> 00:01:54.426
Cole nodded.

34
00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:57.928
"I was going to tell Daisy later that the lollipop was from me.

35
00:01:58.828 --> 00:02:00.149
But then her shirt disappeared!"

36
00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:01.410
He sighed.

37
00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.593
"I was afraid someone saw me near her shirt.

38
00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:08.777
That person could tell Daisy—and make her think that I stole it!"

39
00:02:09.658 --> 00:02:10.458
Henry sighed.

40
00:02:10.478 --> 00:02:14.542
"Why didn't you just say so in the first place?"

41
00:02:14.562 --> 00:02:16.243
"I don't know."

42
00:02:16.624 --> 00:02:17.765
Cole looked sheepish again.

43
00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:20.167
"I thought I could find the shirt myself.

44
00:02:21.128 --> 00:02:23.710
That way nobody would ever know about the candy and stuff."

45
00:02:24.831 --> 00:02:25.532
Henry nodded.

46
00:02:26.216 --> 00:02:29.018
Now he understood why Cole had been acting so strange all day.

47
00:02:29.939 --> 00:02:34.263
The trouble was, Cole's explanation didn't explain what had happened to Daisy's shirt.

48
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:38.666
"So you have no idea how the shirt got into the water trough?"

49
00:02:38.886 --> 00:02:39.427
he asked.

50
00:02:39.447 --> 00:02:41.749
"Nope." Cole shook his head.

51
00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.691
Normally Henry wouldn't doubt his best friend.

52
00:02:45.332 --> 00:02:47.253
But Cole had told a lot of lies today.

53
00:02:48.194 --> 00:02:50.356
Still, he wanted to trust his best friend.

54
00:02:50.376 --> 00:02:53.338
"Maybe it's a red herring," he muttered.

55
00:02:53.358 --> 00:02:54.559
"A what?"

56
00:02:54.859 --> 00:02:55.400
Cole said.

57
00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.961
"A red herring," Henry said.

58
00:02:57.981 --> 00:03:02.042
"That's something that seems like a clue, but isn't.

59
00:03:02.523 --> 00:03:03.563
Like that blue stain.

60
00:03:04.543 --> 00:03:06.044
Maybe it's just a coincidence.

61
00:03:06.964 --> 00:03:12.507
Maybe Rebecca—or someone else—grabbed the shirt without even noticing the lollipop in the pocket."

62
00:03:13.387 --> 00:03:15.108
"That makes sense," Cole agreed.

63
00:03:16.168 --> 00:03:17.769
Henry frowned as he kept thinking.

64
00:03:18.789 --> 00:03:21.831
"But in that case, what happened to the lollipop?

65
00:03:22.771 --> 00:03:24.852
It wasn't in the pocket when we found the shirt.

66
00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.814
And I didn't see it in the water trough."

67
00:03:28.895 --> 00:03:31.157
"Maybe a horse ate it," Cole suggested.

68
00:03:32.098 --> 00:03:34.260
Henry thought about Big Spot's blue slobber.

69
00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:42.247
"Maybe. But why would someone steal the shirt and then leave it in such an obvious place?"

70
00:03:42.527 --> 00:03:43.067
he asked.

71
00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:49.213
"If Rebecca was trying to ruin things for Daisy, Rebecca would have found a better hiding spot for

72
00:03:49.233 --> 00:03:49.673
the shirt.

73
00:03:50.654 --> 00:03:52.356
This just doesn't make sense."

74
00:03:53.472 --> 00:03:56.094
Henry had the feeling he was missing some important clue.

75
00:03:56.974 --> 00:03:58.415
But he couldn't figure out what it was.

76
00:03:59.595 --> 00:04:00.496
He glanced around.

77
00:04:01.316 --> 00:04:04.158
Everyone was gathering near the ring to watch the next class.

78
00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:07.000
There were no lemonade customers in sight.

79
00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.962
"Let's go check the scene of the crime again," he suggested.

80
00:04:10.982 --> 00:04:13.023
"Okay," Cole said.

81
00:04:13.043 --> 00:04:15.844
"Listen, I'm sorry I didn't tell you earlier.

82
00:04:16.445 --> 00:04:17.625
About the lollipop, I mean."

83
00:04:17.645 --> 00:04:19.346
"That's okay."

84
00:04:20.127 --> 00:04:21.568
Henry led the way toward the barn.

85
00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:28.222
When Henry and Cole entered, Cole went over to Maggie, who was near Big Spot's stall.

86
00:04:29.183 --> 00:04:32.284
Henry saw Coco in her stall, though Daisy was nowhere in sight.

87
00:04:33.285 --> 00:04:35.606
Instead Rebecca was standing there patting the pony.

88
00:04:35.626 --> 00:04:37.767
"Hi," said Henry.

89
00:04:37.787 --> 00:04:42.050
"Did you notice the clothes that were hanging on this stall earlier?"

90
00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:45.311
"Clothes?" Rebecca rubbed Coco's nose.

91
00:04:45.331 --> 00:04:47.452
"No. Why?"

92
00:04:47.473 --> 00:04:50.634
"There was a show shirt—" Henry began.

93
00:04:51.575 --> 00:04:53.736
Before he could finish, Cole hurried over to Henry.

94
00:04:54.364 --> 00:04:56.205
"Excuse us," Cole said to Rebecca.

95
00:04:57.006 --> 00:04:58.166
Then he pulled Henry away.

96
00:04:58.186 --> 00:05:01.888
"That's not where Daisy's shirt was hanging!"

97
00:05:02.088 --> 00:05:02.729
he whispered.

98
00:05:02.749 --> 00:05:05.150
"Yes, it was," Henry said.

99
00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.951
"That's Daisy's pony right there.

100
00:05:08.852 --> 00:05:13.394
Her show coat was hanging there too, until she put it on for her last class."

101
00:05:14.375 --> 00:05:15.475
Cole looked confused.

102
00:05:15.495 --> 00:05:16.796
"It was?

103
00:05:17.837 --> 00:05:20.618
But I saw Daisy's shirt hanging on that stall over there."

104
00:05:21.539 --> 00:05:23.700
Cole pointed to the stall next to Big Spot's.

105
00:05:24.704 --> 00:05:26.725
Kira's pony was standing there, looking out.

106
00:05:27.826 --> 00:05:30.587
Henry looked at Kira's pony, and then slowly he smiled.

107
00:05:30.607 --> 00:05:34.350
"Let's go find Daisy," he told Cole.

108
00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:38.192
"I think I know exactly what happened to her shirt."
